<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Direct (Developer ID) distribution: deliberately NOT sandboxed.

         The Mac App Store variant must be sandboxed and can therefore only see
         folders the user explicitly grants. A directly distributed disk
         visualizer is expected to survey whole volumes, so this build relies on
         the user granting Full Disk Access in System Settings, Privacy and
         Security instead. That is a TCC grant, not an entitlement.

         Notarization requires the hardened runtime, which package_app.sh
         applies whenever SIGNING_MODE=identity. DiskX needs none of the
         hardened runtime exceptions: no JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no
         dyld environment variables, no library validation opt out. An empty
         dictionary is therefore the correct and most restrictive entitlement
         set here. Do not copy entries over from DiskX-AppStore.entitlements,
         whose security scoped bookmark keys are inert outside the sandbox.

         Note: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, which is why the
         codesign flags are described in prose above rather than quoted. -->
</dict>
</plist>
